# Rebound playground settings.
#
#   Copy-Item playground\.env.example playground\.env      (PowerShell; then edit playground\.env)
#
# examples/playground/.env is gitignored: put your real key there, never in this file. Exactly ONE provider
# block below must be active (uncommented); the built-in fake model is active by default.
# Write values without quotes and without a comment on the same line.
#
# Provider URLs and models checked against each provider's official docs on 2026-10-11. Models come
# and go: if a model is refused, the UI shows the provider's message; pick a current one in the
# provider's model list.

# Port of the UI on this machine: http://localhost:8090 (8080 is often taken).
DEMO_PORT=8090

# Keep redis: the two app instances share the stream log through it.
REBOUND_STORE=redis

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Built-in fake model: no key, no cost. Streams a canned text word by word (about a minute).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LLM_PROVIDER=fake
# Pause between words in milliseconds, and how many times the text repeats.
FAKE_DELAY_MS=120
FAKE_REPEAT=2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI. Key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# gpt-6-luna: the lowest-priced text model on developers.openai.com/api/docs/models; its model page
# lists Chat Completions and streaming.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-your-key
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-6-luna

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Groq. Key: https://console.groq.com/keys
# Base URL from console.groq.com/docs/openai. openai/gpt-oss-20b streamed through the playground in
# a manual test on a free account (2026-10-11); llama-3.1-8b-instant answered HTTP 404 there.
# llama-3.3-70b-versatile is a slower alternative: it leaves more time to reload the tab
# mid-answer. Groq's docs list stream_options but do not say whether include_usage is
# supported, so usage reporting is turned off here (LLM_STREAM_USAGE=0).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=gsk_your-key
# LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# LLM_STREAM_USAGE=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenRouter. Key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Base URL from openrouter.ai/docs/quickstart. meta-llama/llama-3.1-8b-instruct is listed by
# openrouter.ai/api/v1/models at $0.05 / $0.08 per million input / output tokens. OpenRouter adds
# usage to every stream by itself and does not document stream_options, so it is not sent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-or-your-key
# LLM_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.1-8b-instruct
# LLM_STREAM_USAGE=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Gemini, OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Base URL from ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/openai; gemini-3.5-flash-lite is a stable Flash-Lite
# model on ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models. Gemini answers HTTP 400 (not 401) to a bad key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
# LLM_API_KEY=your-gemini-key
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ollama on this PC (docs.ollama.com/api/openai-compatibility). First: ollama pull llama3.2
# host.docker.internal reaches the host from the containers. Ollama ignores the key, but the
# example requires one: any value works. Not verified on this machine: if the app cannot reach
# Ollama, start Ollama with OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0 so it listens beyond localhost.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=ollama
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.2
